From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] search: the on-screen keyboard is not an outside press

Search closes on a press outside its painted surfaces. Its captured-event
handler runs before ModalDialog's, which routes the on-screen keyboard's
events while the dialog holds the grab, so the first key typed into the
field closed Search instead. Keyboard events are routed first.

--- a/js/ui/lumaSearch.js
+++ b/js/ui/lumaSearch.js
@@ -60,6 +60,12 @@ class LumaSearchDialog extends ModalDialog.ModalDialog {
             if (event.type() !== Clutter.EventType.BUTTON_PRESS &&
                 event.type() !== Clutter.EventType.TOUCH_BEGIN)
                 return Clutter.EVENT_PROPAGATE;
+            // The on-screen keyboard types into the field: its keys, strip
+            // and popups are outside the painted surfaces but are not an
+            // outside press. This handler runs before ModalDialog's own
+            // captured-event handler, which would otherwise route them.
+            if (Main.keyboard.maybeHandleEvent(event))
+                return Clutter.EVENT_STOP;
             const [x, y] = event.get_coords();
             // Only painted surfaces are inside search. The wrapper includes
             // transparent padding and the gap between the field and results.
